{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"platforms":["Linux"],"tokens":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"minimumSpanningTree"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"weight"},{"kind":"text","text":": ("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Edges","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","identifier":"doc:\/\/GraphProtocols\/documentation\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/Edges-swift.associatedtype"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Index","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"SpanningForest","preciseIdentifier":"s:13SpanningTrees0A6ForestV","identifier":"doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees\/SpanningForest"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"AdditiveArithmetic","preciseIdentifier":"s:s18AdditiveArithmeticP"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Comparable","preciseIdentifier":"s:SL"}],"languages":["swift"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"anchor":"discussion","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Edges are ordered by weight, then by position in "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"edges"},{"type":"text","text":". Under that order the minimum"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"spanning forest is unique, and this is it. Its edges are listed in nondecreasing weight"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"and, among equal weights, in position order, and the weight is added up in that order."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Sparse graphs (fewer than 4 edges per vertex) run Kruskal’s algorithm; denser ones run"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Prim’s under the same order and sort the edges taken."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"weight","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" gives each edge’s weight from its position, so parallel edges can differ. It is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"called once for each edge that is not a self-loop and is not kept. Negative, zero and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"infinite weights are ordinary weights. A NaN weight traps; filter such edges out first."}]},{"style":"note","type":"aside","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"O(m log m)."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"Complexity"},{"style":"note","type":"aside","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"No weight is NaN; the sum of the chosen weights, in the order listed, does"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"not overflow and is not NaN."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"Precondition"}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/spanningtrees\/graphprotocols\/graph\/minimumspanningtree(weight:)"]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"sections":[],"metadata":{"remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/SpanningTrees\/Kruskal.swift#L21","fileName":"Kruskal.swift"},"externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P13SpanningTreesE07minimumC4Tree6weightAD0C6ForestVyxqd__Gqd__5Edges_5IndexQZXE_ts18AdditiveArithmeticRd__SLRd__lF","roleHeading":"Instance Method","title":"minimumSpanningTree(weight:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"minimumSpanningTree"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"weight"},{"kind":"text","text":": ("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","text":"Edges"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa","text":"Index"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:13SpanningTrees0A6ForestV","text":"SpanningForest"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"role":"symbol","extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","symbolKind":"method","modules":[{"relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"],"name":"SpanningTrees"}]},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/minimumSpanningTree(weight:)"},"kind":"symbol","hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees","doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees\/GraphProtocols","doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees\/GraphProtocols\/Graph"]]},"abstract":[{"text":"A minimum spanning forest: one minimum spanning tree per connected component.","type":"text"}],"references":{"doc://SpanningTrees/documentation/SpanningTrees":{"role":"collection","kind":"symbol","title":"SpanningTrees","url":"\/documentation\/spanningtrees","abstract":[],"type":"topic","identifier":"doc:\/\/SpanningTrees\/documentation\/SpanningTrees"},"doc://SpanningTrees/documentation/SpanningTrees/GraphProtocols/Graph/minimumSpanningTree(weight:)":{"role":"symbol","title":"minimumSpanningTree(weight:)","kind":"symbol","url":"\/documentation\/spanningtrees\/graphprotocols\/graph\/